{%- comment -%}
  The one place a composed product card decides *which* option it is standing
  on and *which variant* it therefore prices, adds and links to.

  Price and Add need the same initial answer but cannot share a variable. A
  theme block is an isolated render scope, so each starts from
  `closest.product`. An Option control uses the same resolver in Automatic
  mode, or passes its own merchant-selected name/position when drawing a
  targeted row. Each row then publishes the resolved variant for the browser
  to keep the other card parts in sync.

  A snippet cannot hand a value back, so it **prints** and the caller captures
  and splits — the same shape as `space-step.liquid`.

      {%- capture card_option_raw -%}
        {% render 'card-option', product: product, source_mode: block.settings.target_by, source_name: block.settings.option_name, source: block.settings.option_position %}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign card_option = card_option_raw | strip | split: '||' -%}
      {%- assign opt_index = card_option[0] | plus: 0 -%}

  Prints `index||value||variant_id`:

    index      the option's position in `product.options_with_values`, or -1
               where the card stands on no option at all.
    value      the value that position currently carries, or empty.
    variant_id the variant the card prices and adds.

  **The initial variant is Shopify's selected-or-first-available variant.**
  Merchant variant order therefore remains authoritative and a generic theme
  never invents a preference for the most expensive size, colour, flavour, or
  material.

  Price and Add blocks call it with the default for their initial variant. An
  Option control may nominate a position for the row it draws; every value in
  that row carries its resolved variant id and complete option values so the
  browser can move every sibling display and action onto the same variant.

  Accepts:
    product     - product object.
    source_mode - 'auto' (default), 'name', or 'position'.
    source_name - the merchant's exact option name when mode is 'name'.
    source      - a 1-based option position when mode is 'position'.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign opt_index = -1
  assign opt = blank

  comment
    A nominated position is taken as given. `auto` prefers the first option
    that carries a native Shopify swatch; where none does, it uses the first
    option in the merchant's own order. This works for Colour, Material,
    Flavour, Size, or any other naming convention without a translated-name
    table baked into the theme.
  endcomment
  assign target_mode = source_mode | default: 'auto'

  if target_mode == 'name'
    assign wanted_name = source_name | strip | downcase
    if wanted_name != blank
      for option in product.options_with_values
        assign candidate_name = option.name | strip | downcase
        if candidate_name == wanted_name
          assign opt = option
          assign opt_index = forloop.index0
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  elsif target_mode == 'position'
    assign want = source | plus: 0 | minus: 1
    for option in product.options_with_values
      if forloop.index0 == want
        assign opt = option
        assign opt_index = want
        break
      endif
    endfor
  else
    for option in product.options_with_values
      assign option_has_swatch = false
      for option_value in option.values
        if option_value.swatch.color != blank or option_value.swatch.image != blank
          assign option_has_swatch = true
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if option_has_swatch
        assign opt = option
        assign opt_index = forloop.index0
        break
      endif
    endfor

    if opt == blank and product.options_with_values.first != blank
      assign opt = product.options_with_values.first
      assign opt_index = 0
    endif
  endif

  if opt.values.size < 1
    assign opt = blank
    assign opt_index = -1
  endif

  assign current = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign value = ''
  if opt_index >= 0
    assign value = current.options[opt_index]
  endif

  assign chosen = current | default: product.variants.first
-%}
{{- opt_index }}||{{ value }}||{{ chosen.id -}}
